        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/20/ai-fakes-a-growing-problem-on-apple-books-some-written-in-a-few-hours/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/AI-fakes-a-growing-problem-on-Apple-Books-and-Amazon.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Tech writer Joanna Stern wrote last month about discovering 10 fake versions of her book <em>I Am Not a Robot</em> on <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/apple-books/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Apple Books</a> within days of the real thing being published. While she was able to get these removed, new ones quickly appeared.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">New York Times journalist Kashmir Hill found a fake biography of herself on Amazon, and discovered this was one of thousands of <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/artificial-intelligence/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">AI</a>-written biographies available on sale … </p>",
