        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/19/apples-scrapped-mac-pro-plans-reportedly-included-an-intel-model/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/03/mac-pro-rip.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In March, Apple <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/03/26/apple-discontinues-the-mac-pro/\">announced</a> it was discontinuing the Mac Pro and confirmed that it had no plans to offer future Mac Pro hardware.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A new report from <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/newsletters/2026-07-19/why-apple-s-openai-lawsuit-doesn-t-mention-jony-ive-ai-recording-at-genius-bar-mrrv4mix?srnd=undefined\"><em>Bloomberg</em></a> today offers more context on Apple’s Mac Pro strategy, with a surprising tidbit on something Apple was working on … </p>",
