        "title": "Apple unveils new film from ‘Best Picture’ Oscar winner",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/20/apple-unveils-new-film-from-best-picture-oscar-winner/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2025/08/apple-tv-logo.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple made history in 2022 when its film <a href=\"https://tv.apple.com/movie/coda/umc.cmc.3eh9r5iz32ggdm4ccvw5igiir?itscg=30200&amp;itsct=tv_box_link&amp;mttnsubad=umc.cmc.3eh9r5iz32ggdm4ccvw5igiir&amp;at=1000l3cvR\">CODA</a> won the Oscar for Best Picture. And now, the director’s follow-up title—Being Heumann—has just been dated for Apple TV.</p>",
